  "body": "Support SVG and MathML namespaces for `<template>` elements\n\nAllow `<template>` elements to parse their template contents in the HTML, SVG, or MathML namespace, either explicitly via `contentnamespace` or implicitly from their context:\n\n- Add the enumerated `contentnamespace=\"html|svg|mathml\"` content attribute (disallowed in XML documents) and `HTMLTemplateElement.prototype.contentNamespace` reflection, and allow `contentnamespace` in the built-in safe default Sanitizer configuration.\n- `shadowrootmode` supersedes `contentnamespace`.\n- Allow `<template>` elements as children of SVG elements (other than `script` and `style`) and MathML elements (ignored for MathML content models, layout, and rendering).\n- When `contentnamespace` is in no state (missing or invalid), resolve the namespace purely at parse time across `<svg>`/`<math>` ancestors, `<template for>` patch targets, and fragment/streaming parsing into the HTML, SVG, or MathML namespace, tracked per active parser in `parser template namespace map` with no extra `<template>` element state or cloning steps.\n- Fix a `<template>`'s parser contents namespace when the parser pushes it onto the stack of open elements; `prepare content patching` (`<template for>`) only overrides it when `contentnamespace` was in no state and the template remains the current node.\n- Treat HTML and MathML text integration points as HTML-namespace contexts (checking live `encoding` on `<annotation-xml>` outside an active HTML parser), and clamp other or null namespaces to HTML when inherited by `<template>` (leaving non-`<template>` fragment contexts unchanged).\n- Automatically inferred namespaces don't survive serialization on their own.\n- Keep `<template/>` non-self-closing in foreign content and stop foreign end-tag recovery at open `<template>` boundaries (preserving HTML fallback at non-`<template>` fragment roots).\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63892.\n\nCloses #12976\nCloses #3563\n---\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63892 (tentative)\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 16, 2026, 10:40 AM UTC (81a735a)\">/dynamic-markup-insertion.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...81a735a/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 16, 2026, 10:40 AM UTC (81a735a)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 16, 2026, 10:40 AM UTC (81a735a)\">/embedded-content-other.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...81a735a/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 16, 2026, 10:40 AM UTC (81a735a)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/indices.html